To: Roche, Brian J <brian.roche@eversource.com>
Cc: Herman, Robert F <robert.herman@eversource.com>; Rosenburg, Michael P <=
michael.rosenburg@eversource.com>; Sojan, Rosa <rosa.sojan@eversource.com>
Subject: STA 360 Estimate Questions


Brian,



Got some questions fired at me for the STA 360 estimate, see responses belo=
w.  I=92m sure you=92ll have more, feel free to give me a call.



Also =96 Working with Siemens on the breaker estimate, they gave a +/-30% e=
stimate at 300k each.  That would be for the breaker, frame, disconnects, P=
Ts, relays, and battery.



Questions from ES Estimating Group as the PM team has requested a revised e=
stimate based on the most recent scope :

Please check the dollar amount below, all from previous estimate E-23-373.

  1.  Battery System - $12,106,850.
     *   Assuming this is the DC Battery for Control this will be captured =
in the Breaker estimate
  2.  Transportation/Spare Parts - $585,688.
     *   unknown
  3.  Battery labor - $2,553,828, 16,801 mhrs is this for the entire new SS=
 or just for the batteries?
     *   Not sure what this is
  4.  PCS Units - $832,022 is this for the batteries or is this the cost fo=
r the five outdoor standalone feeder cabinets?
     *   Not sure what this is =96 may be a carry over for the PCS for the =
BESS
  5.  Step up transformers - $630,371.
     *   Is this Station Service Transformers or GSUs?
  6.  Site Sound Mitigation - $466,766 - is this done? Do I need to include=
 the estimate?
     *   I would carry this as a risk item if its needed or not
  7.  Rental - Spot Generator - $139,700 - Did not see in scope but is incl=
uded in est. E-23-373, Include in Est. or not?
     *   I don=92t this this is needed =96 we are going to put station serv=
ice transforms in first so we should be good

Other questions:

  1.  Is it an overhead cable or bus from the wood riser pole to the Siemen=
s Breaker? Size and length?
     *   Overhead cable -25=92 per phase should cover us on both sides of t=
he breaker
  2.  The three SSVT pad mount transformers, I added three riser structures=
 with foundations. Also add UG cable, 500LF per SSVT.  Let me know if you a=
gree with this.
     *   Should be down to 1 Station Service Transformer pad mount.  500=92=
 is plenty
  3.  On the eight wood riser poles, are the breaker disconnect switches lo=
cated on these poles?
     *   Breaker Disconnects are on the skid for the breaker
  4.  PTs (8 locations each side of the Siemens breaker, 24 total) - are th=
ey installed on the wood riser poles? or on their own steel supports?
     *   PTs are on the breaker skid



Thanks,



Patrick Fitzgerald

Manager =96 Substations Solutions Engineering

